// ever written when a real web-search-grounded AI pass found genuine
// evidence (a company team/about page, a public professional profile, a
// press mention) tying a real name to a role at this specific company.
// `source` is a plain-language description of where it came from (e.g.
// "Company website /about page"); `sourceUrl`, when known, is the actual
// link. `confidence` is the AI's own honest self-assessment (0.0-1.0) of how
// certain this real-name+role pairing is — never a fixed/fabricated number.
